 "_meta": {
  "what_this_is": "Six queries over a 6-doc corpus for a hybrid retrieval pipeline. Each query carries, per doc, a lexical score (term-overlap, like BM25), a dense score (embedding cosine), and a precise score (a cross-encoder reranker stand-in). Three queries are 'exact' -- the answer shares rare terms, so lexical ranks the gold high and dense is weaker. Three are 'paraphrase' -- the answer is worded differently, so dense ranks it high and lexical is weaker. Neither single retriever is enough; the point is that fusing the two rankings (reciprocal rank fusion) recovers the gold for both kinds, and a reranker then lifts it to rank 1. The gold always has the max precise score, so the reranker nails it whenever fusion put it in the pool.",
  "scores_are": "A FIXTURE standing in for real BM25, embedding-cosine, and cross-encoder outputs, authored so recall at each stage is exact and checkable.",
  "format": "rrf_k (RRF constant); queries [{id, gold, kind, docs:{id:{lex,dense,precise}}}]"
